🛰️ Satellite Swarm Communication System

A Satellite Swarm Communication System is a prototype multi-node wireless communication network inspired by distributed satellite swarm concepts. The system consists of multiple Arduino UNO-based satellite nodes, where each node works as both a transmitter (Tx) and receiver (Rx) using nRF24L01 RF transceiver modules.

The system uses multi-hop communication, allowing data to travel from one node to another until it reaches the ground station. Each node has a unique address and can receive, process, and forward data. If a node becomes unavailable, the system attempts to use another available node, demonstrating fault-tolerant and adaptive communication.

The prototype uses Arduino UNO, nRF24L01, AMS1117 3.3V regulator, 10µF capacitor, LED indicators, and a 16×2 I2C LCD at the ground station. The LED indicates data reception at each node, while the ground-station LCD displays the final received information.

Key Features
📡 Multi-node RF communication
🔄 Transmitter + receiver operation at each node
🔗 Multi-hop data forwarding
🛡️ Fault-tolerant communication
🔁 Alternate-node forwarding when a node is unavailable
📟 Ground-station data display
💡 LED-based node activity indication
🆔 Unique address for each node
Hardware

Arduino UNO → nRF24L01 → AMS1117 → LED → 16×2 I2C LCD
